 "equipment_type": "Water-cooled centrifugal chiller controller",
 "applies_to": "Carrier AquaEdge 19DV two-stage centrifugal chillers with the PIC6 controller.",
 "summary": "The 19DV's PIC6 controller speaks BACnet MS/TP on RS-485 port J8 or BACnet IP on Ethernet, plus Modbus RTU/TCP. Commands use paired read (_rd) and write (_wr) objects; the write copies (start/stop, occupancy, control point, demand limit, emergency stop, free cooling, heat/cool select) are marked CMD. The list also includes temperatures, pressures, guide-vane and VFD data, surge and alarm points.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "default_device_instance": 1600001,
 "notes": [
  "The OPTION column marks command objects as CMD; they are mapped here as writable.",
  "The guide prints control-mode state text against BV 66 GENUNIT_CHIL_S_S_wr; treat BV 66 as a plain start/stop command.",
  "No units column; values follow the BACnet Metric Unit setting."
 ],
